N2  - AbstractThe formation of the Qinghai–Tibet Plateau has long been debated, despite the various proxies used to estimate its paleoelevation. Here, we introduce a novel method to calibrate paleoelevation by comparing the fossil and extant plant communities in the Qinghai–Tibet Plateau. Our estimation confirms that the uplift of the plateau was an episodic and heterochronous process. Specifically, the Lhasa Terrane was already elevated by 1 km before the initial India–Asia collision. During the firs
